:PD.Type a number of up to 15 digits. The value must be from 1 to
9999999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CMPJRNIMG/OUTFMT'.Output format (OUTFMT)
:P.The format of the output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTJRN.Create Journal (CRTJRN)
:P.Use the Create Journal (CRTJRN) command to create a journal attached
to a journal receiver.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/JRNRCV'.Journal receiver (JRNRCV)
:P.The journal receiver, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/ASP'.Journal ASP (ASP)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool the object is put in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIBASP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/JRNMSGQ'.Journal message queue (JRNMSGQ)
:P.The journal message queue for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/MNGRCV'.Manage receivers (MNGRCV)
:P.The manage receivers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/DLTRCV'.Delete receivers (DLTRCV)
:P.Whether to delete receivers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/RCVSIZOPT'.Receiver size options (RCVSIZOPT)
:P.The receiver size options for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMVINTENT, *MINFIXLEN, *MAXOPT1, *MAXOPT2,
*MAXOPT3.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/MINENTDTA'.Minimize entry specific data (MINENTDTA)
:P.The minimize entry specific data for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAARA, *FLDBDY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/FIXLENDTA'.Fixed length data (FIXLENDTA)
:P.The fixed length data for this command.
:P.Up to 9 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USR, *PGMLIB, *SYSSEQ, *RMTADR, *THD, *LUW,
*XID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/JRNOBJLMT'.Journal object limit (JRNOBJLMT)
:P.The journal object limit for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MAX250K, *MAX10M.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/JRNCACHE'.Journal caching (JRNCACHE)
:P.Whether to journal caching.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/JRNSTATE'.Journal state (JRNSTATE)
:P.The journal state for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ACTIVE:EPK.
:PD.Active.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STANDBY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRN/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTJRNRCV.Create Journal Receiver (CRTJRNRCV)
:P.Use the Create Journal Receiver (CRTJRNRCV) command to create a
journal receiver.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRNRCV/JRNRCV'.Journal receiver (JRNRCV)
:P.The journal receiver, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRNRCV/ASP'.Journal receiver ASP (ASP)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool the object is put in.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIBASP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRNRCV/THRESHOLD'.Receiver size threshold (KB) (THRESHOLD)
:P.The receiver size threshold (KB) for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
1000000000.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1500000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRNRCV/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTJRNRCV/AUT'.Public authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTJRN.Delete Journal (DLTJRN)
:P.Use the Delete Journal (DLTJRN) command to delete a journal.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTJRN/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTJRNRCV.Delete Journal Receiver (DLTJRNRCV)
:P.Use the Delete Journal Receiver (DLTJRNRCV) command to delete journal
receivers.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTJRNRCV/JRNRCV'.Journal receiver (JRNRCV)
:P.The journal receiver, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTJRNRCV/DLTOPT'.Delete options (DLTOPT)
:P.The delete options for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IGNINQMSG, *IGNTGTRCV, *IGNEXITPGM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPJRN.Display Journal (DSPJRN)
:P.Use the Display Journal (DSPJRN) command to display, print or write
to a file the entries of a journal.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/FILE'.Journaled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLFILE.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/RCVRNG'.Range of journal receivers (RCVRNG)
:P.The range of journal receivers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*CURCHAIN:EPK.
:PD.The receivers of the current chain.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Ending receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/FROMENT'.Starting sequence number (FROMENT)
:P.The starting sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 20 digits. The value must be from 1 to
18446744073709551600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/TOENT'.Ending sequence number (TOENT)
:P.The ending sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 20 digits. The value must be from 1 to
18446744073709551600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/NBRENT'.Number of journal entries (NBRENT)
:P.The number of journal entries for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 1 to
2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/JRNCDE'.Journal codes (JRNCDE)
:P.The journal codes for this command.
:P.Up to 16 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTL.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Journal code
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Selection
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLSLT, *IGNFILSLT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/ENTTYP'.Journal entry types (ENTTYP)
:P.The journal entry types for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*RCD:EPK.
:PD.The record.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/JOB'.Job (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/CMTCYCID'.Commit cycle identifier (CMTCYCID)
:P.The commit cycle identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 20 digits. The value must be from 1 to
18446744073709551600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/DEPENT'.Dependent entries (DEPENT)
:P.The dependent entries for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/FROMTIME'.Starting date and time (FROMTIME)
:P.The starting date and time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 000000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/TOTIME'.Ending date and time (TOTIME)
:P.The ending date and time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 000000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/OUTFILFMT'.Output file format (OUTFILFMT)
:P.The output file format for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TYPE1:EPK.
:PD.Type 1.
:PT.:PK.*TYPE2:EPK.
:PD.Type 2.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TYPE3, *TYPE4, *TYPE5.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/ENTDTALEN'.Entry data length (ENTDTALEN)
:P.The entry data length for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 32766.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OUTFILFMT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/NULLINDLEN'.Null value indicator length (NULLINDLEN)
:P.The null value indicator length for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PK.*VARLEN:EPK.
:PD.Varying length.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits. The value must be from 1 to 8000.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OUTFILFMT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/INCENT'.Include entries (INCENT)
:P.The include entries for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONFIRMED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRN/FMTMINDTA'.Format minimized data (FMTMINDTA)
:P.Whether to format minimized data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPJRNRCVA.Display Journal Receiver Attr (DSPJRNRCVA)
:P.Use the Display Journal Receiver Attr (DSPJRNRCVA) command to display
a journal receiver's attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRNRCVA/JRNRCV'.Journal receiver (JRNRCV)
:P.The journal receiver, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJRNRCVA/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDJRNPF.End Journal Physical File (ENDJRNPF)
:P.Use the End Journal Physical File (ENDJRNPF) command to end
journaling of physical files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRNPF/FILE'.Physical file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRNPF/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRNPF/LOGLVL'.Logging level (LOGLVL)
:P.How much of the job's messages are written to the job log, from 0
(none) to 4 (all).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ERRORS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCVJRNE.Receive Journal Entry (RCVJRNE)
:P.The Receive Journal Entry (RCVJRNE) command works with a journal's
entries handed one at a time to an exit program in IBM's *TYPEn layouts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/EXITPGM'.Program to receive entries (EXITPGM)
:P.The program to receive entries for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/FILE'.Journaled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLFILE.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/RCVRNG'.Range of journal receivers (RCVRNG)
:P.The range of journal receivers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*CURCHAIN:EPK.
:PD.The receivers of the current chain.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting journal receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Ending journal receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/FROMENT'.Starting sequence number (FROMENT)
:P.The starting sequence number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 15 digits. The value must be from 1 to
9999999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/FROMTIME'.Starting date and time (FROMTIME)
:P.The starting date and time for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Starting time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/TOENT'.Ending sequence number (TOENT)
:P.The ending sequence number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 15 digits. The value must be from 1 to
9999999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/TOTIME'.Ending date and time (TOTIME)
:P.The ending date and time for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Ending date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Ending time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/NBRENT'.Number of journal entries (NBRENT)
:P.The number of journal entries for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be at least 1.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/JRNCDE'.Journal codes (JRNCDE)
:P.The journal codes for this command.
:P.Up to 16 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTL.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Journal code value
:P.The value must be A, B, C, D, E, F, J, L, M, P, R, Q, S, T, U, Y.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Journal code selection
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLSLT, *IGNFILSLT, *IGNOBJSLT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/ENTTYP'.Journal entry types (ENTTYP)
:P.The journal entry types for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*RCD:EPK.
:PD.The record.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/JOB'.Job name (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.User&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Number&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters. The value must be from 000000 to 999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/CMTCYCID'.Commit cycle identifier (CMTCYCID)
:P.The commit cycle identifier for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 15 digits. The value must be from 1 to
9999999999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/DEPENT'.Dependent entries (DEPENT)
:P.The dependent entries for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/ENTFMT'.Entry format (ENTFMT)
:P.The entry format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TYPE1:EPK.
:PD.Type 1.
:PT.:PK.*TYPE2:EPK.
:PD.Type 2.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TYPE3, *TYPE4, *TYPEPTR, *JRNENTFMT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/NULLINDLEN'.Null value indicators length (NULLINDLEN)
:P.The null value indicators length for this command.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENTFMT.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Field data format
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*VARLEN:EPK.
:PD.Varying length.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 8000.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Variable length field length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 8000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/DELAY'.Delay time (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Delay time value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NEXTENT.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Maximum delay time value
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The value of the class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/INCENT'.Include entries (INCENT)
:P.The include entries for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONFIRMED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/JRNENTFMT'.Journal entry format (JRNENTFMT)
:P.The journal entry format for this command.
:P.The value must be RJNE0100, RJNE0200.
:P.When no value is given, RJNE0100 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/RTNPTR'.Return pointers (RTNPTR)
:P.The return pointers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYSMNG, *USRMNG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/BLKLEN'.Block length (BLKLEN)
:P.The block length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 32 to 4000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/FROMENTLRG'.Starting large sequence number (FROMENTLRG)
:P.The starting large sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/TOENTLRG'.Ending large sequence number (TOENTLRG)
:P.The ending large sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/CCIDLRG'.Commit cycle large identifier (CCIDLRG)
:P.The commit cycle large identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAARA, *DTAQ, *LIB.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Member, if data base file
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/OBJPATH'.Objects (OBJPATH)
:P.The objects for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/PATTERN'.Name pattern (PATTERN)
:P.The name pattern for this command.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pattern
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVJRNE/FMTMINDTA'.Format minimized data (FMTMINDTA)
:P.Whether to format minimized data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVJRNCHG.Remove Journaled Changes (RMVJRNCHG)
:P.Use the Remove Journaled Changes (RMVJRNCHG) command to remove
journaled changes from files, backward through a range of entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/FILE'.Journaled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLFILE.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/RCVRNG'.Range of journal receivers (RCVRNG)
:P.The range of journal receivers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PK.*CURCHAIN:EPK.
:PD.The receivers of the current chain.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Ending receiver
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/FROMENT'.Starting sequence number (FROMENT)
:P.The starting sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 20 digits. The value must be from 1 to
18446744073709551600.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/TOENT'.Ending sequence number (TOENT)
:P.The ending sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 20 digits. The value must be from 1 to
18446744073709551600.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LASTSAVE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/FROMTIME'.Starting date and time (FROMTIME)
:P.The starting date and time for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 000000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/TOTIME'.Ending date and time (TOTIME)
:P.The ending date and time for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Date
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Time
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 000000 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/CMTBDY'.Stop at commitment boundary (CMTBDY)
:P.Whether to stop at commitment boundary.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/OBJERROPT'.On object error (OBJERROPT)
:P.The on object error for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CONTINUE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVJRNCHG/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDJRNE.Send Journal Entry (SNDJRNE)
:P.Use the Send Journal Entry (SNDJRNE) command to write a user entry to
a journal.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDJRNE/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDJRNE/TYPE'.Entry type (TYPE)
:P.The entry type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDJRNE/FILE'.Journaled file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDJRNE/ENTDTA'.Entry data (ENTDTA)
:P.The entry data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, ' ' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDJRNE/FORCE'.Force to auxiliary storage (FORCE)
:P.Whether to force to auxiliary storage.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRJRNPF.Start Journal Physical File (STRJRNPF)
:P.Use the Start Journal Physical File (STRJRNPF) command to start
journaling changes to physical files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRNPF/FILE'.Physical file to be journaled (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRNPF/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRNPF/IMAGES'.Record images (IMAGES)
:P.The record images for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRNPF/OMTJRNE'.Journal entries to be omitted (OMTJRNE)
:P.The journal entries to be omitted for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPNCLO.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRNPF/LOGLVL'.Logging level (LOGLVL)
:P.How much of the job's messages are written to the job log, from 0
(none) to 4 (all).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ERRORS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRN.Work with Journal (WRKJRN)
:P.Use the Work with Journal (WRKJRN) command to work with journals and
their recovery options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRN/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRN/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRNA.Work with Journal Attributes (WRKJRNA)
:P.Use the Work with Journal Attributes (WRKJRNA) command to work with a
journal's attributes, receivers and objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRNA/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRNA/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CURATR, *RCVDIR, *JRNFILE, *JRNAP, *JRNDTAARA,
*JRNDTAQ, *JRNLIB, *JRNIFS, *JRNOBJ, *RMTJRN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRNA/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKJRNRCV.Work with Journal Receivers (WRKJRNRCV)
:P.The Work with Journal Receivers (WRKJRNRCV) command works with the
journal receivers of one library or more.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJRNRCV/JRNRCV'.Journal receiver (JRNRCV)
:P.The journal receiver, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
